    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` and wrote a 32-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 32. The implementation follows `spec.md`: it normalises `/` and `\\` separators, drops empty and `.` segments, and resolves `..` against a stack so that any climb above the destination is rejected even if it comes back down later. It also rejects NUL characters, absolute paths, drive prefixes, and members that normalise to nothing. Directory entries are validated but left out of the result. File members are checked for case-insensitive collisions, and results come back in input order. Any unsafe member raises before anything is returned, so no partial plan is produced. The `UnsafePathError` class and the function signature are unchanged, and no other files were created.\n\nTwo judgement calls where the spec was silent: a non-string `dest` also raises `ValueError`, and `\"/\"` and `\"//\"` both map to root (`\"/name\"`). I did not add a check for a file and a directory sharing a path (e.g. `a` and `a/b`), since the spec doesn't mention it.",
